    <sys:String x:Key="AboutTitle">About Alchemy Stars</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutLogoDescription">Alchemy Stars application icon</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutSubtitle">CAST animation merging and Maya 2025 workflow for first-person weapon assets</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutOverviewTitle">Overview</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutOverview">Alchemy Stars is a Windows x64 desktop tool continuously improved from Scobalula/Alchemist. It combines view hands, weapons, attachments, and animation into one CAST file; every export retains one baked target animation ready to play, edit, and continue working with in Maya.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutFeaturesTitle">Key capabilities</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutFeatureFiles">Import through file browsers, editable or pasteable path fields, targeted drag and drop, or context menus; new animations keep output blank until explicitly chosen, preventing accidental source replacement</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutFeatureLayers">Normal, Additive, Gesture, and Gesture Pose layers, frame offsets, and left/right hand IK</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutFeatureModels">One merged model with hierarchy-aware bone identities: weapon roots stay separate from same-name wrist helpers; skinning and animation share the mapping</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutFeatureMaya">Exports full-scene or animation-only CAST, FBX, SMD, and SEAnim; supports relevant-bone-only baking; includes the Maya CAST importer, standard MP5/Hawk examples, and bilingual guides</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutValidationTitle">Compatibility and validation</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="AboutValidation">Maya 2025 regression covers Hawk, 1911 and P27: weapon parenting, skinning, full/selective/animation-only CAST, FBX and SMD. Weapon transforms are compared with separately imported source rigs and animations.</sys:String>
